  "material_learning": "Oldest-open-lot age is broad, causal, decision-time available and capable of lowering measured drawdown, but the frozen veto removes profitable DRA participation rather than isolating low-value entries. The 720-hour rule reduced Validation drawdown by 2.552796 percentage points yet also reduced Validation realized and total PnL by 30.03325733 USDT, doubled maximum underwater duration from 2397 to 4899 hours, won total PnL in only one of five annual folds and concentrated all positive annual delta in 2022. Both rejection-only neighbors also reduced Validation total and realized PnL. Lower drawdown caused by suppressing return is not risk-adjusted alpha.",
